  "events": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "kind": "workspace_created",
      "payload": "{\"base_commit\":\"3438e9678d94eed73e2ff06da2987afc715b24b6\",\"protocol_id\":\"02c5e645b74ca24bbc1fdeba30c474a87ccff24603acebea9fa06987addba601\"}",
      "created": 1792281301.6760747
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "kind": "archive_protocol_identity",
      "payload": "{\"comparison_arm\":\"source-only\",\"effort\":\"max\",\"internal_harness_enabled\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-6.1-sol\",\"mother_enabled\":true,\"operator_algorithm_advice\":false,\"shared_preparation_sha256\":\"9e9d303f6a1ba154a9bc2c255ecaeaf726345ae90e73c7d89df6bd97527c8be2\"}",
      "created": 1792281301.6914482
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "kind": "F_retrieval",
      "payload": "{\"characters\":0,\"documents\":[],\"llm_tokens\":0,\"query\":\"A locality SIMD OpenMP\"}",
      "created": 1792281301.9651165
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "kind": "mother_usage",
      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"preparation\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Research successor-generation costs while retaining player-step BFS and existing traversal order. Precompute legal directional neighbors from the parsed board. Compare repeated box scans against an occupancy/index scratch map built once per expanded state, using touched-cell clearing or stamps. Exploit the invariant that box coordinates are sorted: walking needs no sorting; pushing needs only removal/reinsertion of the moved box, not bubble sort. Preserve canonical keys, push legality and parent links. Benchmark incremental variants because preprocessing and scratch-map maintenance may outweigh savings on this short workload. Do not introduce fixed board/box limits or collapse distinct player positions.\",\"B\":\"Research visited-table and allocation efficiency. Start with the missing full-hash comparison before memcmp. Investigate better hash mixing for power-of-two buckets and deterministic incremental hashing of the player plus box set; retain full state equality checks for collisions and treat zero hashes correctly. Compare chaining with a compact open-addressed table. Probe a scratch candidate before allocating persistent storage, and consider append-only slabs instead of constructing free lists for duplicate candidates. Keep parent/queue references stable and state strides correctly aligned for ARM64. Preserve first-visit and queue order. Measure simple changes separately from larger layout redesigns.\",\"C\":\"Research sound search-space pruning without changing the movement objective or BFS schedule. The existing live mask already supplies union-of-goals reverse-push reachability; avoid merely duplicating it. Begin with local, completely blocked 2x2 wall/box patterns containing an off-goal box. A more ambitious branch may compute per-goal reverse-push reachability and reject box arrangements lacking a matching covering every box with distinct reachable goals, consistent with the existing success predicate. Evaluate expensive checks only when boxes change and consider caching by box arrangement. Supply a soundness argument for every rejection rule. Never prune using unproved freeze heuristics, and retain a cheap variant if stronger checks lose to setup overhead.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only measured, correct programs from the research trees. Retain the baseline and best standalone candidate; evaluate combinations within the existing budget rather than assuming gains add. Use the unchanged compiler, target, tests, oracle and timing procedure. Preserve reference generation order, layer reversal, first-visit behavior and output formatting. Check interactions between occupancy scratch state, box reinsertion, incremental hashes, pruning and stable arena references. Require correctness reasoning beyond the four observed cases. Compare end-to-end timings, account for the roughly 0.07 ms observed baseline spread, and prefer the simpler candidate when differences are inconclusive. Do not add parallel startup overhead merely to use four cores; retain the baseline if no reliable improvement survives integration.\",\"analysis\":\"The optimization target is Problem C, src/sokoban.c. The baseline passed four cases and averaged 4.5656 ms, with samples spanning 4.5393–4.6094 ms; there is no profiling evidence or measured optimization yet. On four-core ARM64 without GPUs, low-overhead serial improvements are the first priority, although fixed overhead may limit end-to-end gains. Source-level opportunities include repeated occupancy scans, unnecessary sorting, collision-chain comparisons and allocation work for duplicate states. Correctness includes shortest total player movements, not minimum pushes. The statement requests U/D/L/R tie ordering, whereas the source generates R/L/U/D and prepends each next layer. Treat that discrepancy as a correctness risk: preserve the accepted reference traversal during optimization rather than silently changing tie behavior or the oracle.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"12f41aa31614ff4b4f8aa24d335a393bef7e11ef5e510f2e27251067fa67a126\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Research successor-generation costs while retaining player-step BFS and existing traversal order. Precompute legal directional neighbors from the parsed board. Compare repeated box scans against an occupancy/index scratch map built once per expanded state, using touched-cell clearing or stamps. Exploit the invariant that box coordinates are sorted: walking needs no sorting; pushing needs only removal/reinsertion of the moved box, not bubble sort. Preserve canonical keys, push legality and parent links. Benchmark incremental variants because preprocessing and scratch-map maintenance may outweigh savings on this short workload. Do not introduce fixed board/box limits or collapse distinct player positions.\",\"B\":\"Research visited-table and allocation efficiency. Start with the missing full-hash comparison before memcmp. Investigate better hash mixing for power-of-two buckets and deterministic incremental hashing of the player plus box set; retain full state equality checks for collisions and treat zero hashes correctly. Compare chaining with a compact open-addressed table. Probe a scratch candidate before allocating persistent storage, and consider append-only slabs instead of constructing free lists for duplicate candidates. Keep parent/queue references stable and state strides correctly aligned for ARM64. Preserve first-visit and queue order. Measure simple changes separately from larger layout redesigns.\",\"C\":\"Research sound search-space pruning without changing the movement objective or BFS schedule. The existing live mask already supplies union-of-goals reverse-push reachability; avoid merely duplicating it. Begin with local, completely blocked 2x2 wall/box patterns containing an off-goal box. A more ambitious branch may compute per-goal reverse-push reachability and reject box arrangements lacking a matching covering every box with distinct reachable goals, consistent with the existing success predicate. Evaluate expensive checks only when boxes change and consider caching by box arrangement. Supply a soundness argument for every rejection rule. Never prune using unproved freeze heuristics, and retain a cheap variant if stronger checks lose to setup overhead.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only measured, correct programs from the research trees. Retain the baseline and best standalone candidate; evaluate combinations within the existing budget rather than assuming gains add. Use the unchanged compiler, target, tests, oracle and timing procedure. Preserve reference generation order, layer reversal, first-visit behavior and output formatting. Check interactions between occupancy scratch state, box reinsertion, incremental hashes, pruning and stable arena references. Require correctness reasoning beyond the four observed cases. Compare end-to-end timings, account for the roughly 0.07 ms observed baseline spread, and prefer the simpler candidate when differences are inconclusive. Do not add parallel startup overhead merely to use four cores; retain the baseline if no reliable improvement survives integration.\",\"analysis\":\"The optimization target is Problem C, src/sokoban.c. The baseline passed four cases and averaged 4.5656 ms, with samples spanning 4.5393–4.6094 ms; there is no profiling evidence or measured optimization yet. On four-core ARM64 without GPUs, low-overhead serial improvements are the first priority, although fixed overhead may limit end-to-end gains. Source-level opportunities include repeated occupancy scans, unnecessary sorting, collision-chain comparisons and allocation work for duplicate states. Correctness includes shortest total player movements, not minimum pushes. The statement requests U/D/L/R tie ordering, whereas the source generates R/L/U/D and prepends each next layer. Treat that discrepancy as a correctness risk: preserve the accepted reference traversal during optimization rather than silently changing tie behavior or the oracle.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-6.1-sol\",\"nonce\":\"65cff8955867439bab87399c1a2d1848\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"max\",\"request_sha256\":\"12f41aa31614ff4b4f8aa24d335a393bef7e11ef5e510f2e27251067fa67a126\",\"session_id\":\"665743a02b824021a697b6a4884a667c\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"ac0191cb0886eaf99d42cb243bdc03200a87440580beabf35e5529e0690a1a35\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"input_tokens\":13714,\"output_tokens\":5383,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":4660}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-6.1-sol\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"max\",\"token_accounting\":\"exact\",\"tokens\":19097,\"tool_events\":[]}},\"status\":\"complete\"}",
